{
    "background_story": "Aspen, a young and adventurous traveler, had always been fascinated by the rich cultural heritage of India. Her journey took her to the eastern state of Odisha (formerly known as Orissa), where she spent several months immersing herself in the local way of life. She marveled at the stunning sunrises over the Konark Temple, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and spent hours exploring the vibrant streets of Puri. Aspen was particularly drawn to the traditional Odia crafts, and she spent many days learning the intricacies of sand art and Pattachitra painting from local artisans. As she delved deeper into the culture, she discovered a sense of belonging and connection to the land and its people. Aspen's experiences in Orissa left an indelible mark on her, and she returned home with a newfound appreciation for the diversity and beauty of Indian culture.",
